            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0313" n="215" xml:id="pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11299: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-19T12:00:00+08:00">November 19,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 19—10:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>121. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 19, noon. The U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Tutuila</hi> fired
                            upon by rifle fire at mileage 27 above Chenglingki yesterday. Fire
                            silenced with 27 rounds 3-inch shells and 650 rounds machine gun.
                            Repeated to Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
